---
const dialogue = [
  {
    label: 'Developer',
    text: 'We need organization-level API keys. I think we should add a new keys table and expose CRUD endpoints.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Agent',
    text: 'I inspected the existing credential path. Personal tokens already use a shared secret model, encrypted storage, scoped permissions, and revocation events. A parallel keys table would duplicate three contracts.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Developer',
    text: 'Organization keys need independent rotation and must never inherit a user’s access after that user leaves.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Agent',
    text: 'Then the existing secret model can remain the storage owner, but principal type and organization ownership must become explicit. Rotation belongs in the credential service; membership removal should not revoke organization-owned keys.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Together',
    text: 'Extend the established credential boundary, add organization ownership and authorization, preserve one rotation flow, and cover revocation, role changes, and duplicate requests before implementation.',
  },
] as const;
---

<ol class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border bg-border">
  {
    dialogue.map(({ label, text }, index) => (
      <li
        class:list={[
          'grid gap-3 bg-background p-5 sm:grid-cols-[8rem_1fr] sm:p-7',
          label === 'Together' && 'bg-accent/8',
        ]}
        tabindex="0"
      >
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs font-bold text-muted">0{index + 1}</span>
          <span class:list={['text-sm font-extrabold', label === 'Agent' && 'text-accent']}>
            {label}
          </span>
        </div>
        <p class="max-w-3xl text-base leading-7 sm:text-lg sm:leading-8">{text}</p>
      </li>
    ))
  }
</ol>
